  <h2>About the service</h2>
  <p>Plate &amp; Bar is a tracking tool for meals and workouts, run by [operator name]. It is still in development and not yet released. By using the app or this website you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use them.</p>

  <h2>Who can use it</h2>
  <p>The app is for adults aged 18 and over. If you are under 18, do not create an account or use the app.</p>

  <h2>Not medical advice</h2>
  <p>The app gives general fitness and nutrition guidance. It does not provide medical advice, diagnosis or treatment.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The health check in the app is a screen, not a diagnosis. It can only point out that you may want to talk to a doctor first. A result with no flags does not mean exercise is safe for you.</li>
    <li>If you have a medical condition, are pregnant, or are unsure whether exercise or a diet change is safe for you, check with a qualified professional first.</li>
    <li>Calorie, protein and other targets are estimates. Stop and seek advice if something hurts or feels wrong.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>break the law or use the service to harm others;</li>
    <li>try to get into another person's account or data;</li>
    <li>probe, overload or disrupt our server, or get around rate limits and the shared AI budget;</li>
    <li>copy, scrape or resell our server's content in bulk, other than as the content licence below allows;</li>
    <li>upload anything you do not have the right to use.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your content and licences</h2>
  <p>What you log (meals, workouts, weights, notes, your own foods and recipes and similar) is yours. You give us only the permission needed to store it, sync it between your devices and show it back to you. Progress photos, cycle data and lab results stay on your device and are not uploaded.</p>
  <p>Our own content (such as exercise descriptions, cards and recipes written for the app) is licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0). The app's source code is licensed under the Apache License 2.0. Third-party material, such as fonts and food data, stays under its own licence. See the <a href="/licenses/">licences page</a>.</p>

  <h2>AI features</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>AI features are off by default. They run only after you switch them on yourself, and you can switch them off at any time.</li>
    <li>AI output is information, not advice. It can be wrong, incomplete or out of date. Check it before you act on it, and do not use it in place of a doctor, dietitian or coach.</li>
    <li>What is sent to an AI service is described in the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Accounts and sync</h2>
  <p>The app works without an account. If you sign in (by email code or Google), you are responsible for keeping access to that email or Google account secure and for what happens under your sign-in. If you agree to sync, your records are also stored on our server so they appear on your other devices. If two devices change the same record, we keep one version and a copy of the other, as the privacy policy explains.</p>

  <h2>Deleting your account</h2>
  <p>You can delete your account at any time from "Your data" in the app. Deleting removes your account and its server data straight away, with no undo. See <a href="/delete-account/">how to delete your account</a> and the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for what is and is not deleted. We may also suspend or close an account that breaks these terms.</p>

  <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>The service is provided as is and as available. We may change, pause or stop any part of it, and we do not promise it will always be available or free of errors. We may update these terms; the date of the latest version will be shown on this page, and continued use after a change means you accept it. If a change is material we will tell you in the app.</p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for any loss or injury that comes from relying on the app, its targets or its AI output, or from data loss, downtime or sync conflicts. Nothing in these terms limits any liability that cannot be limited by law, or any right you have under law. [Liability cap and wording to be settled with legal review.]</p>

